---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Studio payments: firing fees, class packs and memberships"
	description="Charge firing fees by cubic inch, sell class packs and gift cards, and bill memberships from the same place you run your kilns and classes."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Studio payments</p>
				<h1>Get paid for every firing, class and pack.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Firing fees, class packs and memberships usually live in three different places. In
					Kilnbook, members pay at the moment they log a piece or book a seat, so the kiln log and the
					payments are the same record.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/class-pack.svg"
				alt="A six-class pack card with three classes used and a waitlist card for a Tuesday evening session"
				width="480"
				height="320"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Firing fees, charged when the piece is logged</h2>
		<p>
			Set a rate per cubic inch, a flat fee per piece, or both. Members enter the size of their piece
			(or pick one of your presets) and pay right then, before it goes on the shelf. Nobody has to
			measure pots or chase payments at the end of the month.
			<a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Class packs and gift cards</h2>
		<p>
			Sell a pack of 5 or 10 classes and students spend one credit per drop-in, with an expiry date
			you choose. Gift cards can be for any amount or for a specific course. Instructors see who has
			paid right on their roster. <a href="/features/classes">Classes and packs</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Memberships</h2>
		<p>
			Membership tiers decide how many wheel hours each member gets and how far ahead they can book.
			Recurring membership billing sits in the same place as firing fees and class packs, so you are
			not spending weekends reconciling a paper kiln log with a payment app.
		</p>

		<h2>The small fees, too</h2>
		<p>
			Charge a storage fee for pieces left on the pickup shelf too long, or a fee for a missed wheel
			booking. You decide which fees apply and when, so the awkward conversations don't have to happen
			at the front desk.
		</p>

		<h2>What it costs</h2>
		<p>
			Starter is $29 a month, Studio is $79 and Collective is $149, billed monthly in USD. Every
			studio starts with a 30-day free trial, and no card is needed. <a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
</Base>
